The regression we hit at the moment is that activemq enforces TomEE to import jackson whereas it wants to keep johnzon as JSON mapper impl. Since JSON-B spec is out and implemented by both I guess it can be the way to solve that issue.

The most blocking thing is ./activemq-broker/src/main/java/org/apache/activemq/broker/jmx/DestinationsViewFilter.java - which can already not create a mapper if json is empty ;) - but here is the list of code location which would be neat to fix:

